<title>USA: US Senate passes oil/gas pipeline safety bill.</title>
<headline>US Senate passes oil/gas pipeline safety bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. House was expected to vote shortly on an oil and natural gas pipeline safety bill after the Senate passed the measure late Thursday.</p>
<p>The bill, which was backed by the pipeline industry and passed on a voice vote, would require federal regulators to make more use of risk assessment and cost-benefit evaluations.</p>
<p>The Office of Pipeline Safety, which also is funded through industry user fees under the bill, supported the measure after changes were made in it to make the evaluations less burdensome on the agency.</p>
</text>
